      "content": "You mentioned \"higher statistical risk associated with urban residency\" and \"community stability.\" Could you expand on that? If a judge were looking at a defendant from an urban area vs a suburban area, what specific factors or data points would they use to justify a harsher sentence for the urban resident? I want to make sure I understand the nuances of how \"risk of recidivism\" is applied in these different contexts for my exam.",
